<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Rävala</h1><p class="st-meta">800 CE – 1219 CE (approx.) · capital Lindanise</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Coastal Estonian county around Lindanise, the site of modern Tallinn, conquered by King Valdemar II of Denmark in 1219.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Rävala occupied the northern coast of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-estonia">Estonia</a> around the bay where <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/reval">Tallinn</a> now stands. A harbour and stronghold at Lindanise served Baltic shipping, and the Arab geographer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-al-idrisi">al-Idrisi's</a> 1154 map may record it as a town called Qlwry. The county appears in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-of-livonia">Henry of Livonia's</a> chronicle in the early 13th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its elders controlled the harbour and the trade passing between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scandinavia">Scandinavia</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/grand-duchy-of-finland">Finland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veliky-novgorod">Novgorod</a>. The county farmed the coastal plain and kept close ties with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/harjumaa">Harjumaa</a> inland. Little else is known of its institutions.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1219 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valdemar-ii-of-denmark">Valdemar II of Denmark</a> landed with a crusading army, defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonians">Estonians</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lindanise">Battle of Lindanise</a> and built a castle on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toompea">Toompea</a>; legend places the falling of the Danish flag, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flag-of-denmark">Dannebrog</a>, from the sky at this battle. Rävala became the core of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-estonia-1219-1346">Duchy of Estonia</a> (1219-1346), and Lindanise grew into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/reval">Reval</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ravala.jpg" alt="Rävala" width="320" height="219"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. 藏骨集团 assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_Estonian_counties.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>800 CE – 1219 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lindanise</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Estonian paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Estonian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/estonia">Estonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Revalia, Rävala county</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1010&amp;focus=ravala" aria-label="Rävala on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5207 184 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Rävala lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5527 440L5521 437"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5521 437h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5527 440h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5527 440h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1010&amp;focus=ravala">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
